(1,'KEEP',[I],'theory','Discrete and continuous walking under a fully supplied watch-hand rule','All angular/time rules and step conventions are printed. Summed rotations, complex geometric/Gauss sums, periodicity and continuous curvature equations classify trajectories using kinematics and mathematics only.'),
(2,'KEEP',[I],'theory','Tangential versus radial force to start a uniformly loaded disk moving','Uniform carpet pressure and circumferential pull geometry are explicit. Distributed static-friction limit and force/torque balance about the incipient rotation centre determine the threshold ratio without a microscopic contact theory.'),
(3,'KEEP',[I],'theory','Frictional Y-branch anchors supporting a log stack','Actual support/stack diagram, insertion depth, friction rules and negligible log-log friction are given. Force moments, thrust from packed rigid logs and Coulomb anchor friction constrain support heights and maximum stack height.'),
(4,'KEEP',[I],'numerical','Aircraft trajectories under a specified constant felt vertical acceleration','The felt 1g load condition, initial speed/height and allowed planar/cylindrical geometry define a Newton constrained acceleration problem. Differential path/energy integration determines trajectories and impact speed; inner-ear physiology is only the stipulated sensing premise.'),
(5,'KEEP',[I,II],'theory','Weak control of an unstable pivoted rod under a known train acceleration','Rod/pivot model, bounded weak force, known acceleration and finite experiment with selectable start are given. Newton torque/inverted-pendulum ODE and stability/control mathematics determine whether falling can be prevented.'),
