(8,'KEEP',[I],'numerical','Wire sag after a bird of specified relative weight lands centrally','Span, initial sag and bird weight in units of wire length are given. Ordinary flexible-string force balance/catenary geometry and length conservation determine new sag under a declared inextensible or measured axial-elastic approximation.'),
(9,'KEEP',[I],'theory','Residual axial strain/stress in a bonded steel-concrete composite','Initial longitudinal stretch, long bonded geometry and released end force define ordinary scalar axial Hooke compatibility and total force balance. Material moduli/areas/prestrain remain parameters; a full radial tensor solution is not explicitly requested as the dominant work.'),
(10,'BORDERLINE',[I,III],'experimental','Observed inflation shape of an initially cylindrical balloon','Gas pressure, membrane force/geometry and measured shape supply substantial ordinary experimental reasoning. A predictive large-strain shape/localization explanation can centrally require an unsupplied nonlinear rubber stress-stretch law. No supplied constitutive model or intended approximation resolves the whole-task boundary.'),
(11,'KEEP',[I],'theory','Qualitative pipe size comparison under material-dependent flow resistance','The short why question can be answered by ordinary pressure-loss/roughness/deposit reasoning and declared pressure/flow demand. It does not mandate an unsupplied quantitative turbulent friction correlation or microscopic corrosion calculation.'),
(12,'KEEP',[X],'theory','Two images in a stationary parabolic flashlight reflector','Actual mirror size/depth and switched-off observation are provided. Parabolic ray reflection and finite observer/object geometry produce multiple local image branches; no relativistic moving mirror is involved.'),
